#: includes/admin.php:234
#: includes/admin.php:685
msgid "WP Masking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:235
msgid "Hides the WordPress structure in the pages visitors receive. The web server maps the new paths back to the real files; the rules are part of tegatai-nginx.conf (nginx) or of the Tegatai block in .htaccess (Apache, LiteSpeed)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:239
msgid "Hide plugin and theme paths"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:239
msgid "Plugin and theme folders are shown under their own names, e.g. /assets/bar/ instead of the plugin folder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:240
msgid "Hide wp-includes, wp-json and admin-ajax"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:240
msgid "wp-includes, the REST API and admin-ajax.php get their own paths. /wp-json/ keeps working for The Hive and other sites."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:241
msgid "Remove versions and identifiers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:241
msgid "Removes ?ver= parameters, script/style ids, generator tags, RSD/wlwmanifest/shortlink/REST links, the emoji script, the speculation rules (they list the WordPress paths) and the X-Pingback header."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:242
msgid "Hide file names"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:242
msgid "File names of masked plugin, theme and wp-includes files are replaced by a neutral name per file, e.g. /assets/bar/css/t3f9a0c1d2e4. The folders stay, so relative URLs in CSS and JS keep working. A changed file gets a new name."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of active file names, 2: number of waiting file names
#: includes/admin.php:247
#, php-format
msgid "File names: %1$d active, %2$d waiting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:248
msgid "New files are found when pages are visited. Tegatai adds them to the rules and checks them every hour; they are used as soon as the web server knows the rules (nginx: after a reload; Apache and LiteSpeed: at once). \"Check new paths\" does both right away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:251
msgid "Block original paths"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:251
msgid "Visitors get a 404 for the original paths of masked entries. Logged-in users keep access. /wp-json/tegatai/ (The Hive) stays reachable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:254
msgid "How it is activated"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:255
msgid "1. Switch on and save the names. 2. nginx: reload nginx so the new rules are active (Apache and LiteSpeed read the .htaccess at once). 3. Click \"Check new paths\". Only paths that answered correctly are used in the pages and blocked, so a missing reload never breaks the site."
msgstr ""

